# 11. TAX MANAGEMENT

Implement configurable tax rules.

Each tax rule should support:
- Tax name
- Tax rate
- Tax type
- Description
- Active/inactive status

Support tax rules at the appropriate product or invoice-line level.

Do not hardcode 18% tax.

The system must:
- Calculate taxes from configured rules.
- Apply the correct tax to invoice items.
- Calculate subtotal and final total accurately.
- Preserve the applied tax rate and amount in historical invoices.
- Prevent accidental modification of historical invoice calculations.

Use appropriate decimal precision for financial calculations.

Avoid JavaScript floating-point errors in monetary calculations. Use decimal arithmetic or integer minor currency units consistently.

